      {
        "review_id": 382867770,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r382867770-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "If not Hindu, maybe not worth it",
        "text": "It's an interesting place, but if you are not Hindu, you will not be allowed to actually enter the temple. They will allow you to walk almost to the door and take a picture, and then they tell you about a \"back door\" where you can see everything. Not so! You can go around the back and see some cremations, but you still cannot actually see anything inside the temple. Considering the price (about $10) this made me more than a little frustrated. Furthermore, despite saying so on the sign, locals do not have to pay. So, the only people paying for the temple are the ones who can't even go in!\n\nAlso, guides will chase you and try to tell you about the place even after you say no, monkeys are aggressive (I accidentally looked at one as I walked near it and it ran toward me to attack, but stopped when I turned my back to it), and lots of people will try to get money from you in some way or another.\n\nI give it two stars because you can walk around outside and there are some interesting things to see, but I would never go back and sort of felt that I had wasted my time.",
