        "title": "Must to be visited temple for heritage",
        "text": "One of the heritage hindu temple in the world where still the priest from south India appointed as a priest. It is at walkabale distance from Kathmandu Airport (hardly 2 KMS). This is a UNESCO heritage site. The temple is good, peaceful and as soon as you enter, You feel the divine touch and calmness. You are not allowed to take any photo, so be careful. You will find many shops outside where you can buy original rudraksh (considered to be part of Shiva) garland.  Just behind the temple is a flowing river where people do ritual/ last rite which is not a happy scene. Beware from monkeys there ",
