      {
        "review_id": 380135954,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r380135954-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Interesting but high entrance fee!",
        "text": "The entrance fee to this temple is 1000 rupees for foreigners. When I went, I saw many people just walked in and out of the temple freely but as soon as I entered, a \"tourist police\" stopped me and said I have to pay entrance fee. When I asked why the others do not need to pay even though it says so on the board, he merely said because I am obviously a tourist. So tip to avoid entrance fee would be to dress local and look local maybe. I point this out because I see many people walk in without paying. Anyway, the temple itself is very interesting - many stories, histories to learn and things to see. There are two places where they burn the dead bodies and usually they burn about 2.5 hours to 3 hours depending on their sex. There are fertility temples and an old sacrificial temple too which is no longer in use. A man who works there approached me as I was sightseeing the place and started giving me information about the places, I really appreciate the info he gave me and while I did not ask for his help, I decided to tip him anyway when I left. Instead of being grateful however, he lamented the tip was too little. The tip was definitely not little for such a short time of \"service\" but his response gave me a sour feeling throughout the rest of my day. Hope others wont have similar experience!",
